Psalm 119:49-56

49 Remémber your wórd to your sérvant,
by which you máde me hópe.
50  Thís is my cómfort in sórrow:
that your prómise gives me lífe.

51 Though the próud may útterly deríde me,
I do not túrn from your láw.
52 When I remémber your júdgments of óld,
thése, O LÓRD, consóle me.

53 I am séized with indignátion at the wícked
who forsáke your láw.
54 Your státutes have becóme my sóng
wheréver I dwéll.

55 I remémber your náme in the níghttime,
and I kéep your láw.
56 Thís has been my lót,
for I have képt your précepts.

Glóry to the Fáther, and to the Són,
and to the Hóly Spírit:
as it wás in the begínning, is nów,
and will be for éver. Amén.
